---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { PROFILE } from '../data/profile';
import { TOOLS } from '../data/tools';
import { loadContentIndex } from '../lib/content';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { webPageSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const { articles, categories } = await loadContentIndex();
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'About' },
];
const jsonLd = [
  webPageSchema(
    'About ORIZ.IN',
    'What ORIZ.IN is, how it is built, who publishes it, and the principles behind its tools and articles.',
    '/about/',
  ),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ORIZ.IN"
  description="ORIZ.IN is an independent, static-first knowledge and tools library built by Chirag Singhal. Learn what it offers, how it is made, and how it is funded."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container">
    <PageIntro
      eyebrow="About"
      title="A small, independent library for useful work."
      description="ORIZ.IN is a place for clear explanations and working browser tools. It is not a content farm, a social network, or a disguised lead-generation funnel."
      meta={[
        `${TOOLS.length} local tools`,
        `${articles.filter((entry) => !entry.data.noindex).length} published articles`,
        `${categories.length} populated categories`,
      ]}
    />

    <div class="page-body">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          ORIZ.IN collects two kinds of useful things: articles that explain a
          concept or a workflow, and tools that actually perform the task the
          page describes. A formatter formats. A calculator calculates. A
          reference is searchable. Nothing is published as “available” until it
          works.
        </p>
        <p>
          The initial library covers web development, data formats, networking,
          personal finance, mathematics, design, accessibility, and developer
          references. It is designed to grow without turning every new article
          into a new page architecture or every new calculator into a separate
          application.
        </p>

        <h2>What it is not</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It is not a publisher of invented reviews, ratings, or visitor statistics.</li>
          <li>It is not a financial adviser. Calculators are educational models, not recommendations.</li>
          <li>It is not a secure vault. The tools run locally, but they are not designed for secrets.</li>
          <li>It is not a promise that a third-party API will remain available or unchanged.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Static first.</strong> Pages are pre-rendered and served as
          files. The browser only loads interactive code where it is needed.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Local by default.</strong> Tool inputs are processed in the
          browser. A formatter should not need a server copy of your data.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Registry driven.</strong> Categories, tools, APIs, learning
          paths, and glossary terms come from validated data. Navigation,
          indexes, feeds, and public JSON exports are generated from the same
          source.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Honest limits.</strong> Every tool lists what it does not
          handle. The API directory shows verification dates. The site does not
          promise search rankings, AdSense approval, or unlimited free
          third-party services.
        </p>

        <h2>How it is built</h2>
        <p>
          ORIZ.IN is a statically generated Astro site with selective React
          islands. Content is written in Markdown and stored in Git. Diagrams
          are rendered from text with Mermaid; mathematics is typeset at build
          time with KaTeX. The search index is generated at build time. Data
          endpoints are static JSON files, not a dynamic API service.
        </p>
        <p>
          The production target is Cloudflare Pages' free tier. There is no
          application server, database, account system, or required paid
          service. Analytics and advertising integrations are optional and
          disabled until explicitly configured.
        </p>
        <p>
          The code and content live in the
          {' '}
          <a href={SITE.repoUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">public repository</a>.
          Technical documentation and data endpoints are on the
          {' '}
          <a href="/developers/">developer resources page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
        <p>
          ORIZ.IN is edited and maintained by
          {' '}
          <a href={SITE.authorUrl}>{PROFILE.name}</a>, a software engineer and AI
          engineer based in India. The public author page lists current work,
          selected projects, and contact details. Nothing on this site invents a
          company, an office, an author credential, or a review that does not
          exist.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence and funding</h2>
        <p>
          The site currently has no paywall and no mandatory advertising. It can
          be supported voluntarily through
          {' '}
          <a href={SITE.supportUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Buy Me a Coffee</a>.
          If advertising is enabled later, placements will be labelled and kept
          away from tool controls and primary navigation. Sponsorship or paid
          placement cannot buy a favourable reference entry or a fabricated
          test result.
        </p>

        <h2>Policies and contact</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>,
          {' '}
          <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>, and
          {' '}
          <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>
          {' '}
          describe the details. For corrections, roles, or general questions,
          email
          {' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>
          {' '}
          or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="maker-band" style="margin-top: 2.5rem">
        <div>
          <h2>Work with the person behind it.</h2>
          <p>
            I am open to software engineering and AI engineering opportunities,
            including work on developer tools and AI systems.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="maker-actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--small" href={SITE.authorUrl}>
            Chirag Singhal
            <Icon name="arrow-right" size={15} />
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary btn--small" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
